  "type": "singleCorrect",
  "level": 2,
  "question": {
    "text": "If four distinct points $(2 k, 3 k),(2,0),(0,3)$ (0,0) lie on a circle, then",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "v8uUF",
      "text": "$k     < 0$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "LS26Z",
      "text": "$0     < k < 1$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "LGOks",
      "text": "$k=1$",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "ELL4y",
      "text": "$k>1$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Since, join of (2,0) and (0,3) subtends $90^{\\circ}$ at (0,0)\r\n$\\Rightarrow$ It is a diameter.\r\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/wbjee/2012_mat_a18.png\">\r\n\r\n$\\therefore$ Equation is $(x-2)(x-0)+(y-0)(y-3)=0$\r\n$x^{2}+y^{2}-2 x-3 y=0$\r\n$(2 k, 3 k)$ lies on it $\\Rightarrow \\quad 4 k^{2}+9 k^{2}-4 k-9 k=0$\r\n$\\Rightarrow$\r\n. $13 k^{2}=13 k$\r\n$\\Rightarrow$\r\n$k=1$\r\nsince, $k \\neq 0$ otherwise $(2 k, 3 k)$ will be (0,0)",
    "image": null
  },
